  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your 'Wild cards' (8s and Jokers) for your final few turns. Using an 8 as your last card is the safest way to win because you don't need to worry about the suit on the pile. Save penalty cards (2s, Jokers) for when opponents have few cards.\n\nThe Draw Trap: If a player to your right says 'Last One', and you have a 2 or a Joker, play it immediately! This forces them to draw cards and ruins their chance of winning on their next turn. Also, use 8s strategically to change to a suit where you hold multiple cards.\n\nSuit Control: If you have many cards of one suit and see your opponent keeps drawing when that suit is on top, keep playing that suit. Use your 8 to change back to that suit whenever they manage to switch. Track which special cards have been played to know when it's safe to hold a small hand.",
    Player: "Keep your 'Wild cards' (8s and Jokers) for your final few turns. Using an 8 as your last card is the safest way to win because you don't need to worry about the suit on the pile. Save penalty cards (2s, Jokers) for when opponents have few cards.\n\nThe Draw Trap: If a player to your right says 'Last One', and you have a 2 or a Joker, play it immediately! This forces them to draw cards and ruins their chance of winning on their next turn. Also, use 8s strategically to change to a suit where you hold multiple cards.\n\nSuit Control: If you have many cards of one suit and see your opponent keeps drawing when that suit is on top, keep playing that suit. Use your 8 to change back to that suit whenever they manage to switch. Track which special cards have been played to know when it's safe to hold a small hand.",
